# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is grafana/promtail:3.6.11 (Task #93/Phase 4), which deliberately pins
# older than Loki's own 3.7.10: Grafana has stopped publishing grafana/promtail image builds
# past 3.6.11 (confirmed directly against Docker Hub, not assumed -- the project is being
# wound down in favor of Grafana Alloy). 3.6.11 is the real current latest, so these findings
# cannot be cleared by a version bump the way Loki's were; they're genuine "fixed upstream,
# not yet in a republished image" waivers like the rest of this file.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# apt / libapt-pkg6.0t64, Ubuntu base layer package. Affects: grafana/promtail:3.6.11
CVE-2026-109518

# gpgv (GnuPG), Ubuntu base layer package. Affects: grafana/promtail:3.6.11
CVE-2025-68973

# github.com/docker/docker, vendored as promtail's Docker API client for its docker_sd_configs
# container discovery (read-only: listing containers/labels, never pulling or extracting
# images). Both CVEs describe vulnerabilities in the Docker Engine's own image-pull/extraction
# code path, which promtail's read-only discovery usage never exercises; Trivy still flags the
# vendored client library itself. No fixed version is published upstream yet (FixedVersion:
# None) -- not just "not rebuilt", there is nothing to rebuild against.
# Affects: grafana/promtail:3.6.11
CVE-2026-41567
CVE-2026-42306

# github.com/klauspost/compress, vendored into promtail for log-stream compression. Fixed
# upstream; not yet picked up by a newer promtail image build (none has been published).
# Affects: grafana/promtail:3.6.11
CVE-2026-63209

# github.com/prometheus/prometheus, vendored into promtail (shared scrape-config/service-
# discovery code with the Prometheus project). Fixed upstream; not yet picked up.
# Affects: grafana/promtail:3.6.11
CVE-2026-42151
CVE-2026-42154

